<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uppland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uppland is a historical province of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala">Uppsala</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Svear</a>, the people from whom Sweden takes its name, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamla-uppsala">Old Uppsala</a> was the seat of early kings and a pagan cult centre. It has the largest number of Viking-age runestones in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uppland.jpg" alt="Uppland" width="320" height="729" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lapplänning (highlighting by Lokal_Profil) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sverigekarta-Landskap_Uppland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
